        "# PART 2 — WRAPPER METHOD: RFECV `(25 pts)`\n",
        "\n",
        "A wrapper method **trains the model again and again** on different subsets of features and keeps the subset with the best result.\n",
        "\n",
        "You will use `RFECV`: it removes the weakest feature one at a time (**Recursive Feature Elimination**), checks the accuracy of every subset with **Cross-Validation**, and picks the best **number** of features by itself."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "19c6cfa1",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "19c6cfa1"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 7. Run RFE with Cross-Validation `(8 pts)`\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Create an `RFECV` named `rfecv` with `LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000)` as the estimator, `step=1`, `cv=StratifiedKFold(5)` and `scoring=\"accuracy\"`. `(4 pts)`\n",
        "2. Fit it on `X_train` and `y_train`, and print the best number of features. `(4 pts)`\n",
        "\n",
        "*Hint: the best number of features is in `rfecv.n_features_`.*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 10,
      "id": "b9e0e960",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "b9e0e960",
        "outputId": "5da908e5-fa26-4830-aa47-a6435fb2cbbf",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Best Number of Features: 7\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "estimator_wrapper = LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000)\n",
        "\n",
        "rfecv = RFECV(\n",
        "    estimator=estimator_wrapper,\n",
        "    step=1,\n",
        "    cv=StratifiedKFold(5),\n",
        "    scoring=\"accuracy\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "rfecv.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Best Number of Features:\", rfecv.n_features_)"
      ]
    },
